>> title: Coq au Vin
>> category: Stews & Braises
>> tags: chicken, french, wine, braise, oven
>> counters: Meat and Three
>> aka: coq au vin rouge, chicken in red wine
>> pairs-with: baguette
>> servings: 4
>> time: 2 hr
>> step.5: braise 325°F 1 hr
>> step.7: whisk in

Preheat the #oven{} to 325°F (160°C).

Render @bacon{4%oz}(115 g; cut in lardons) in a #Dutch oven{}.

Brown @chicken thighs{3%lb}(1.4 kg; bone-in, skin-on), @kosher salt{2%tsp} in @&(~1)bacon fat{}.

Soften @pearl onions{16}(peeled), @cremini mushrooms{12%oz}(340 g; halved), @garlic{3%cloves} with @&(~1)browned chicken{}.

Braise @&(~1)pot{} with @dry red wine{3%cup}(710 mL; most of a bottle), @chicken stock{1%cup}(240 mL), @thyme{4%sprigs}, @bay leaf{1} for ~{60%min}.

Mash @unsalted butter{2%Tbs} with @all-purpose flour{2%Tbs}(15 g).

Whisk @&(~1)beurre manié{} into @&(~2)braise{}.
